WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.340
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.197
Most of our decisions whether we like it
or

00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:11.425
not, most of our actions, most of our
behavior,

00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:15.000
most of our experiences are constantly
being shaped at the instinctual level.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.992
I would argue that about 90 to 95% of our
decisions, even important decisions.

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:23.251
You might think that you're being
rational, but

00:00:23.251 --> 00:00:26.692
keep in mind that if you pit the rational
brain against the emotional brain in

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.458
general, it is the emotional brain that is
going to win out.

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:34.742
In fact, I have this quote of David says,
that the irrational brain does not be,

00:00:34.742 --> 00:00:36.780
is not good at being rational.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.178
What it is good at is simply rationalize
what the emotional brain has

00:00:40.178 --> 00:00:41.380
already decided to do.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.561
And therefore,

00:00:42.561 --> 00:00:48.220
it behooves us to understand the workings
of the instinctual emotional brain.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.567
Neuromodulators, like serotonin, dopamine,
cortisol, et cetera,

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.224
have a significant impact on who we are.

00:00:55.224 --> 00:00:55.818
even, for

00:00:55.818 --> 00:00:59.979
example, who we are in the morning
compared to who we are in the afternoon.

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:02.965
And that has a huge significance in terms
of

00:01:02.965 --> 00:01:07.979
the nature of the decisions that we make
in the morning versus in the afternoon.

00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:10.980
[MUSIC]

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.420
The answer to this question is that in
general,

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.958
it is far better off scheduling your
decision making in the morning,

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:20.620
because that's when the levels of, the
natural levels of serotonin.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:24.104
The natural levels of dopamine, serotonin
is the calming chemical,

00:01:24.104 --> 00:01:26.060
dopamine is the excitatory chemical.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.644
Serotonin levels are going to be normal,

00:01:27.644 --> 00:01:30.689
because when you wake up in the morning,
serotonin levels are going to be high.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:35.613
As a result of which, you can start taking
chances, you're less risk averse.

00:01:35.613 --> 00:01:38.426
But as what happens when as the day begins
to progress is

00:01:38.426 --> 00:01:41.500
that there's a natural decline in the
level of serotonin.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.117
As a result of which, when you're making
decisions in the afternoon,

00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:47.000
you will tend to be more risk averse.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.221
And therefore, there'll be a tendency to
gravitate towards what we

00:01:50.221 --> 00:01:52.619
call the status quo, the classic status
quo bias.

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:57.019
And the status quo bias will manifest in
the form of an indecision.

00:01:57.019 --> 00:02:00.451
And that's where you'll see that very
often when you're making decisions,

00:02:00.451 --> 00:02:03.159
important decisions especially, in late in
the afternoon.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:05.985
Very often, you'll end up postponing those
decisions, you know,

00:02:05.985 --> 00:02:07.800
because you like to stick to the status
quo.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.700
[MUSIC]

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.020
Sleep is extremely critical.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.852
Why?
Because there is one phase of sleep called

00:02:14.852 --> 00:02:19.946
deep sleep or slow wave sleep and this is
where our natural levels of serotonin,

00:02:19.946 --> 00:02:22.699
dopamine, et cetera, come back to normal.

00:02:22.699 --> 00:02:25.438
And, therefore, if you don't get good
quality sleep,

00:02:25.438 --> 00:02:29.489
what I mean by that is good quality deep
sleep or slow-wave sleep, you'll likely to

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:32.880
end up in waking up in the morning with
lower levels of, of serotonin.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.440
As a result of which, you're more likely
to be in a type one mindset fearful.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.320
More likely to make decisions out of fear.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.840
More likely to be risk averse, et cetera.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.819
[MUSIC]

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:48.967
Previously, people thought that what
fitness does is it releases endorphins in

00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:52.139
the brain, because we all feel good after,
after a workout.

00:02:52.139 --> 00:02:55.680
Turns out it is really not it's really not
endorphins.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.896
Turns out that it's actually a precursor
to

00:02:58.896 --> 00:03:03.340
serotonin that is released when you are
going through a fitness workout.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.011
And therefore, it is a,

00:03:05.011 --> 00:03:10.279
it's natures way to keep our levels of
serotonin and dopamine during the day.

00:03:10.279 --> 00:03:13.239
[MUSIC]

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:16.389
I always advise people to have a high
protein breakfast, good quality protein.

00:03:16.389 --> 00:03:19.340
It could be a whey protein, it could be
egg protein.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.920
Egg white, for example.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.967
Why?
Because as the day begins to

00:03:22.967 --> 00:03:24.140
progress, right?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.891
You had a breakfast like at seven o'clock
in the morning,

00:03:26.891 --> 00:03:28.360
as the day begins to progress.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.519
All these other amino acids are getting
absorbed past the blood brain barrier.

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:34.616
The one of the last ones to be released
and

00:03:34.616 --> 00:03:38.019
get absorbed is tryptophan, which is a
precursor to serotonin.

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:41.464
So which means that if you had a
high-quality protein breakfast in

00:03:41.464 --> 00:03:45.033
the morning by the time you're hitting
about 11, 11:30 when

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:48.970
you're gonna expect a down is when you're
going to get a serotonin boost and

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.154
therefore, you're effective, as effective
making decisions in the middle of

00:03:53.154 --> 00:03:54.900
the day as you are in the morning.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:04.900
[MUSIC]

